# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# iCloud Drive sync-conflict copies. The repo tree moved to ~/Developer (out of
# ~/Documents) to escape iCloud/OneDrive/Google-Drive collisions; this guard is retained
# as defense-in-depth for any clone that still lands in a cloud-synced folder.
# iCloud mints "<name> 2.<ext>" copies on conflicts (e.g. GitHub Desktop branch switches
# racing the sync), and `git add -A` will silently ingest them. This pattern keeps the
# file-level copies out. If you ever need a legitimately-named "... 2.md" file, add it
# with `git add -f`.
* [0-9].*
# The extensionless form ("<name> 2", no dot) is the one that actually got in: 14 such files
# were tracked before this guard, because `* [0-9].*` requires a dot after the number. The
# earlier note here said we deliberately left it loose to protect directories like "Draft 2/";
# the negation below protects those explicitly, which is cheaper than leaving the hole open.
* [0-9]
!Draft [0-9]/

# Python bytecode cache (e.g. TOOLS/__pycache__ from importing lore_validate in lore_build_manifest).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# LORE workbench — runtime state lives in ~/.lore (or $LORE_HOME), not the repo.
# Guard only against a stray repo-local .lore/. Do NOT ignore *.asc: detached
# signatures (KEYS/*.asc, INTAKE/RAW-MANIFEST.sha256.asc, author-only artifact
# signatures) are tracked and central to the signing workflow.
/.lore/

# Python bytecode (workbench tools)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
